# Workers Assets reads this file from the assets root and does not serve it.
#
# The discovery document is a kill switch, and a kill switch behind an edge
# cache nobody set is a kill switch with an unknown delay. `no-cache` is "hold
# this, but ask before using it" rather than "do not store it" -- the same
# choice, for the same reason, that the API makes on every answer carrying a
# Version. Without it the outage message a human just wrote reaches people
# whenever Cloudflare's heuristics decide it should.
/discovery.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The two installers, held to the same rule and for the same reason. A broken
# installer is the same category of artifact as a stale kill switch: the fix has
# to reach people when it is written, not when Cloudflare's heuristics decide.
# These are also the only files here a person pipes straight into a shell, so
# "the copy you fetched is the copy we published" is worth more than the cache.
#
# Content-Type is stated rather than sniffed. `irm | iex` hands PowerShell
# whatever the response says it is, and an octet-stream body can arrive as bytes
# instead of the string `iex` needs.
/install.sh
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Type: text/x-shellscript; charset=utf-8
/install.ps1
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
